From b2763da2b4ed8042a4e9c8d45e88a4b6e3c50bf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Concerns Workflow Fix <concerns-workflow-fix@local>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 01:57:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Conform Concerns workflow to authoritative spec

KPIs:
- Add kpi_concerns_not_closed, kpi_concerns_total, kpi_concerns_invited,
  kpi_concerns_resolved (card defs, role-scoped overrides, drilldown
  filters, cache scoping).
- kpi_concerns_total is society-wide on every portal (incl. Owner), per
  spec's literal {'all' concerns, society_id} with no apartment_id.
- Rewrite DEFAULT_LAYOUTS + the customize-KPI catalog so every
  portal/tab's KPI set matches the spec table exactly (Admin, Owner,
  Vendor, Security's pass_evaluation/security_concerns tabs).

Workflow buttons:
- Remove Security's Bid/Decline (vendor-only per spec), locked down
  server-side in concern_bid_callbacks.py's BID_ROLE_CODE too.
- Add Admin's Accept (assigned->accepted), Decline (assigned->declined),
  and Resolved (accepted->resolved) actions, incl. new loader functions,
  handlers, and renderer gating.
- Fix Security's Resolved gate to check an ADMIN's row status='accepted'
  on the same concern (loaders.is_any_admin_accepted), per spec, instead
  of security's own assignment status.
- Add matching push notifications for the new admin/security events.

Database:
- Add 'accepted' to concerns_assigns.status; update
  fn_sync_concern_status() to treat it like 'assigned' in the aggregate.
- New migration/rollback pair:
  migration_concerns_assigns_accepted_status.sql,
  rollback_concerns_assigns_accepted_status.sql,
  apply_migration_concerns_assigns_accepted_status.py.
